# Wave W17-Q (Route 122): pyre rock — Requiem shoulder rock standing in the lane’s water: a broad shoulder boulder banded in drowned reds — dark red-brown at the waterline, a pale rust band across its face where the mountain’s iron bleeds — foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it (design: Mt. Requiem rising from the water mid-lane, its keeper’s path climbing from the south shore). Route 122’s own rock — the fleet’s only red-banded rock: split from Route 124’s dark trench rim by colour (rust bands vs blue-grey dark) and from every W17-M rock by the banding itself.
